  "$comment": "Blender-built neat pack models (tools/art/blender/families/pack_neat.py). Replaces the primitive-part placeholders of packs/neat by key; the placeholder is kept as a fallback if a file fails to load, and the materials map onto the game's finishes so a model costs one draw call per finish group. Each moves one part while it is used: the mop leaves its dock, the washer's door opens, the rain falls, a bin slides out, the robot rolls out and the key tray drawer opens.",
